 "_how": "Automatic KEYWORD-checklist hits, not factual accuracy. An item is a hit when EVERY group in 'all' has an alternative in the SAME line of the normalised summary (bullet, table row or paragraph), as whole words with plural/tense endings allowed, and not after a negation in the 4 words before it. An alternative ending in '*' is an explicit word-start prefix. Items and alternatives were built from the scripts before any Meetily output was seen; on 2026-11-01, after review, the five stem alternatives were marked with '*' and the matching rules were tightened (they were global substring matches before). Single-keyword items stay lenient: they do not check amounts, owners or deadlines; the hand audit does.",
